DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Robbie & Torin 425-344-6997\n\n \n\nScope- N NW Corn
	er Unit L5 appears to contain each window typed (two of ea. In unit - Oper
	able & Fixed). There is a potential to test other Units on north elevation
	 at your discretion if the sealant will be finished and  may be closer to 
	water source but that is what is currently ready during the visit.\n\n \n\
	nWater Source:\n\n \n\nWater is on ground level east elevation near sidewa
	lk. The distance is significant and Exxel plants to run a couple hundred f
	eet hose to get you close. I would pack the accelerator pump since the wat
	er pressure will be unknown.\n\nThey will shut off other water use during 
	testing to ensure maximum pressure from the manifold on their spigot.\n\n 
	\n\nPower Source:\n\n \n\nWe advise to ensure there is a power source with
	in an extension cord range for our equipment. \n\n \n\nTest Pressure- \n\n
	 \n\nOnsite contact-\n\n \n\nNick Wilson​​​​\n\n	\nSenior Building
	 Envelope Foreman\n\nBellevue Office\n\n11820 Northup Way #300\n\nBellevue
	\n\n\, \n\nWA\n\n \n\n98005\n\nCell: (253) 228-5975 <tel:(253)%20228-5975>
	 \n\nOffice: (425) 230-5698 <tel:(425)%20230-5698> \n\n \n\n
