DESCRIPTION:Nate\, Torin\, Chris\, Robbie & Jesus W/ BEE 206-409-3240\n\n \
	n\nScope: Whole Building Air barrier testing.\n\nContractor responsibility
	.\n\n*	HVAC will be shut off\, all electronic dampers will be in the close
	d position.\n*	Shut and latch all windows and exterior doors by 12 noon. 
	“ this includes elevator vestibules.”\n*	Empty the bldg. at 12 noon.\n
	*	Locate any louvers and or dampers that are not closed or covered. \n*	Po
	wer – Adequate power to be placed @ selected L1 entry doors associated w
	ith fan placement. \n*	Cargo elevator available for use.\n\nBEE responsibi
	lity\n\n*	Arrive on site @ 7am to begin set up.\n*	Prop all stair well doo
	rs open.\n*	Isolate any louvers and or dampers that are not closed or cove
	red.\n*	Begin testing @ 12 noon.\n*	Finish testing no later than 2pm\n*	Pa
	ck up equipment and get off site.\n*	Fast turnaround on test report or ema
	il of preliminary test results the day after the test.\n\nFan Placement \n
	\n*	6 bank of fans in L1 loading dock double doors- two temp power boxes n
	eeded.\n*	6 bank of fans in L1 lobby double doors - two temp power boxes n
	eeded.\n*	3 bank of fans in L1 Stairwell B exterior door – one temp powe
	r boxes needed.\n\n \n\nPass fail Criteria will be .25 cfms per square foo
	t @ 75pa.\n\n \n\nOn site contact:\n\nGreg Doughty\, Assistant Superintend
	ent \n\nSellen Construction // C 206.450.1030\n\n \n\n
