DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Nate\, Chris\, Jesus & Torin 206-409-3240\n\n \n\nAf
	ter our meeting last week\, it was determined the BLDG is very close to be
	ing ready for the Air Barrier Test.\n\n \n\nWe discussed:\n\n*	BEE will ta
	ke responsibility of the pretest prep. I will be sending a contract over t
	o Red Hawk\, for $20 a unit.\n*	A few exterior thresholds need to be compl
	eted.\n*	The hollow metal door hardware needs to be complete.\n*	One broke
	n vinyl window needs to be fixed or replaced.\n*	All storefront glass need
	s to be completely installed. \n\n \n\nTest Day:\n\n*	BEE will arrive on s
	ite @ 8am to begin prepping the building and setting up the test equipment
	.\n*	The contractor will have the building HVAC shut off and all electroni
	c dampers in the closed position.\n*	The contractor will have the building
	 empty at 12 noon for one hour.\n*	The test will be complete by 1pm. \n*	B
	EE should be off site around 3pm.\n\n \n\nI have sent a tentative schedule
	 of 10/20/23. Please let me know as soon as posable if that works on your 
	end. \n\n \n\n \n\nOnsite Contact-\n\nChanyn Pauole | Project Engineer\n\n
	Redhawk Group <mailto:Redhawk%20Group>  | chanynp@redhawkgroup.com <mailto
	:chanynp@redhawkgroup.com> \n360.536.8601 cell\n\n \n\n
