DESCRIPTION:Attendees: Nate\, Chris\, Robbie\, torin\, Jesus W/BEE 206-409-
	3240\n\n \n\nScope:\n\nBEE will arrive on site @ 8am to begin set up. The 
	GC will have the HVAC shut off by 9am. All electronic dampers will be clos
	ed by the HVAC representative\, BEE will be instructed on any thing that d
	oes not shut electronically so we can mask it off. The GC will have the bu
	ilding empty by 4pm. So\, the test can begin. 8/15/23 is a backup day.\n\n
	 \n\nFan Placement:\n\n6 fans will go in the double doors in the lobby\, t
	hree fans\, will go in the adjacent man door. 3 fans will go in the stair 
	well on the other end of the BLDG. \n\n \n\nPower:\n\nDPR will provide tem
	p power. 3 spider boxes @ the lobby area and one spider box @ the stairwel
	l at the other end of the building. \n\n \n\nElevators:\n\nThe GC will ope
	n the elevator doors from L1 through P1\,P2 & P3 to the non-communicating 
	hallway areas in the parking garage.\n\n \n\nDrawings:\n\nWill be revised 
	using the most current plan set provided by DPR.\n\n \n\nZones:\n\nWe will
	 revise the drawings to zone out the conditioned areas in the parking gara
	ge.\n\n \n\nOn site contact:\n\nChris Allen\, DBIA\, LEED AP (BD+C) | DPR 
	Construction | www.dpr.com <http://www.dpr.com/>  \n\n1000 1st Ave S | Sui
	te 400 | Seattle\, WA | 98134\nm: 206-999-1491\nWe Exist to Build Great Th
	ings.®\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n
