DESCRIPTION:All- we’ll meet for a walk-through as discussed today.\n\n \n
	\nPurpose is to give BEE opportunity to make pre-test observation and enga
	ge DPR\, trade partners\, and Gensler pertaining to whole building air lea
	kage testing scheduled for 8/14/23 at 4:00 PM (BEE’s Nate Van Voorst to 
	issue invitation). We’ll review proposed test fan placement locations\, 
	walk through test zone boundaries\, and observe locations of potential tes
	t isolation measures needed.\n\n \n\nNote- I’ve included all the previou
	s meeting’s invitees as I said I would\, plus added Prime and Gensler pa
	rties. I respect your other commitments and really only need one (or two m
	ax) from PSF\, ATS\, Prime\, and Gensler. You’re all welcome of course.\
	n\n \n\nThanks\,\n\n \n\nChris Allen\, DBIA\, LEED AP (BD+C) | DPR Constru
	ction | www.dpr.com <http://www.dpr.com/>  \n\n1000 1st Ave S | Suite 400 
	| Seattle\, WA | 98134\nm: 206-999-1491\nWe Exist to Build Great Things.®
	\n\n \n\n \n\n
