DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Teams meeting \n\nJoin on your computer\, mobile app 
	or room device \n\nClick here to join the meeting <https://teams.microsoft
	.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_YWMxNDUyOWQtYTNhMS00MzllLWI3ZDUtZTU2ZjBhNz
	A3NGNk%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%223ea4ee53-5e07-4a30-bd0d-e46
	4769a4f4f%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%226ee88ecd-2c9d-46d7-b320-231c20606b98%22%7d> 
	 \n\nMeeting ID: 268 330 721 358 \nPasscode: xAAR5C \n\nDownload Teams <ht
	tps://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-teams/download-app>  | Join on the
	 web <https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-teams/join-a-meeting> \n\nJoin w
	ith a video conferencing device \n\n767302315@t.plcm.vc <mailto:767302315@
	t.plcm.vc>  \n\nVideo Conference ID: 115 061 408 1 \n\nAlternate VTC instr
	uctions <https://dialin.plcm.vc/teams/?key=767302315&conf=1150614081>  \n\
	nOr call in (audio only) \n\n+1 323-892-2559\,\,492634495# <tel:+132389225
	59\,\,492634495#>    United States\, Los Angeles \n\nPhone Conference ID: 
	492 634 495# \n\nFind a local number <https://dialin.teams.microsoft.com/0
	45a7622-d963-4bb2-819b-fd33809f65fc?id=492634495>  | Reset PIN <https://di
	alin.teams.microsoft.com/usp/pstnconferencing>  \n\nLearn More <https://ak
	a.ms/JoinTeamsMeeting>  | Meeting options <https://teams.microsoft.com/mee
	tingOptions/?organizerId=6ee88ecd-2c9d-46d7-b320-231c20606b98&tenantId=3ea
	4ee53-5e07-4a30-bd0d-e464769a4f4f&threadId=19_meeting_YWMxNDUyOWQtYTNhMS00
	MzllLWI3ZDUtZTU2ZjBhNzA3NGNk@thread.v2&messageId=0&language=en-US>  \n\n__
	__________________________________________________________________________
	____ \n\n \n\nThank you for your reply\, Nate. We’d like to review with 
	BEE the project’s plan for Whole Building Air Leakage Testing. We’d li
	ke to begin with an overview of work and the plan. We do have the document
	s you’ve furnished pertaining to pretest conditions and test procedure.\
	n\n \n\nConsidering current work in place\, and plan for remaining work\, 
	DPR anticipates completing whole building air leakage testing August 7-8\,
	 2023. Our current path to enclosure completion enables this\, though we a
	lso are requesting to put a “hold” for potential testing August 14-15\
	, should it be required.\n\n \n\nWe look forward to discussing with you th
	en.\n\n \n\nThanks\,\n\n \n\nChris Allen\, DBIA\, LEED AP (BD+C) | DPR Con
	struction | www.dpr.com <http://www.dpr.com/>  \n\n1000 1st Ave S | Suite 
	400 | Seattle\, WA | 98134\nm: 206-999-1491\nWe Exist to Build Great Thing
	s.®\n\n \n\n_____________________________________________\nFrom: Nate Van
	 Voorst <Nate@bee-engineers.com <mailto:Nate@bee-engineers.com> > \nSent: 
	Thursday\, July 13\, 2023 11:17 AM\nTo: Emma Parks <Emma@westlakeconsultin
	ggroup.com <mailto:Emma@westlakeconsultinggroup.com> >\; David DuBose <Dav
	idDu@dpr.com <mailto:DavidDu@dpr.com> >\nCc: Chris Allen <chris.allen@dpr.
	com <mailto:chris.allen@dpr.com> >\; Michael Pearson <michaelpe@dpr.com <m
	ailto:michaelpe@dpr.com> >\; Joseph Morgan <Joseph.Morgan@dpr.com <mailto:
	Joseph.Morgan@dpr.com> >\; Chris Shafer <Chris@bee-engineers.com <mailto:C
	hris@bee-engineers.com> >\nSubject: RE: 1150 - Air Leakage Testing \n\n \n
	\nI could do it on the morning of the 25th . \n\n \n\nNate Van Voorst\n\nP
	rincipal & Testing Manager | BEE Consulting\n\nD: 425 678-1740 | C: 206 40
	9-3240 | O: 425 672-3900\n\n \n\nFrom: Emma Parks <Emma@westlakeconsulting
	group.com <mailto:Emma@westlakeconsultinggroup.com> > \nSent: Wednesday\, 
	July 12\, 2023 4:40 PM\nTo: Nate Van Voorst <Nate@bee-engineers.com <mailt
	o:Nate@bee-engineers.com> >\; David DuBose <DavidDu@dpr.com <mailto:DavidD
	u@dpr.com> >\nCc: Chris Allen <chris.allen@dpr.com <mailto:chris.allen@dpr
	.com> >\; Michael Pearson <michaelpe@dpr.com <mailto:michaelpe@dpr.com> >\
	; Joseph Morgan <Joseph.Morgan@dpr.com <mailto:Joseph.Morgan@dpr.com> >\nS
	ubject: 1150 - Air Leakage Testing \n\n \n\nHi Nate\,\n\n \n\nHope you’r
	e doing well. Wanted to connect you with the DPR team. I believe they’ve
	 already reached out to you\, and you’ve provided them a pre-pair leakag
	e check list. I wanted to make sure you’re also coordinating a time to d
	o a pre-test walk and pre-test meeting with the team.  Per the latest sche
	dule update air leakage testing is scheduled for 8/14-8/15. DPR has sugges
	ted 7/24 as a day to do a pre-test walk.  I’ll let the team take it from
	 here. \n\n \n\nThank you\, \n\nEmma Parks\n\nTel: 206.351.3220\n\n2825 Ea
	stlake Ave. E.\, Suite 350\, Seattle\, WA 98103\n\nemma@westlakeconsulting
	group.com <mailto:emma@westlakeconsultinggroup.com>  \n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n___
	__________________________________________________________________________
	___ \n\n
