DESCRIPTION: Attendees: Nate Torin & Robbie W/ BEE 206-409-3240\n\n \n\nSco
	pe:\n\nWhole BLDG Air Barrier testing. This project has selected reduced a
	ir infiltration as an energy credit. The maximum leakage rate is .25 cfm
	’s @ 75pa. The Diagrams are attached. The building must pass the test or
	 is subject to retesting.\n\n \n\nPretest meeting Notes:\n\nAt the time of
	 the meeting there was work in progress that needs to finish prior to the 
	test:\n\n*	Cladding @ balcony condition\n*	Storefront entry way installati
	on \n*	Exterior entry way soffit\n*	Exterior Metal door hardware and thres
	holds. \n\n \n\nPretest prep:\n\nBEE will assist the GC in the task of iso
	lating all unit ventilation from the exterior. \n\n*	Two stacks of ventila
	tion hoods on the north elevation can be reached wit the use of a Boom lif
	t supplied by the GC. \n*	Two stacks of ventilation hoods on the east elev
	ation can be reached by pump Jacks. \n*	Two stacks of ventilation hoods on
	 the south elevation can be reached with the use of a Boom lift supplied b
	y the GC.\n*	All other unit ventilation comes out the roof.\n*	BEE will pr
	op open all interior doors.\n\n \n\nHVAC:\n\nThe HVAC system will need to 
	be shut off on the day of the test\, all electronic dampers in the closed 
	position.\n\n \n\nTest Time:\n\n*	The test will begin @ 12 noon.\n*	The GC
	 will empty the building of all Subs for a 1-hour duration. \n*	We will op
	en the BLDG back up @ 1pm. \n\n \n\nOn site contact:\n\nKEITH WOLBRECHT | 
	Project Manager\n\nM  425.866.1074\n\nwww.rmillerinc.com <http://www.rmill
	erinc.com/> \n\n \n\n \n\n
DTEND;TZID="Pacific Standard Time":20230515T160000
