ATTENDEE;CN="Robbie Smith";RSVP=TRUE:mailto:Robbie@bee-engineers.com
CATEGORIES:Window Testing
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20231212T230638Z
DESCRIPTION:Robbie & Torin\, w/ BEE 425-595-7654\n\n \n\nTest pressure:\n\n
	6.0 psf. All window products Test no less than 5 window products.  \n\n \n
	\nJob #:\n\n2003-1005\n\n \n\n \n\nInspection Notes:\n\nWhile on-site BEE 
	discussed the window water testing requirement with the general contractor
	. The windows in units 425\, 423\, and 419 were selected for testing and t
	he nearest water source is available at the Southwest corner of the site. 
	Please contact the Testing Manager Nathan Van Voorst to schedule the testi
	ng Phone # 425-672-3900 or Cell # 206-409-3240 or Nate@bee-engineers.com <
	mailto:Nate@bee-engineers.com>  at least 3 weeks in advance of the preferr
	ed test date. Prior to testing\, the contractor shall\; invite the window 
	manufacturer to the fenestration test and make sure the window manufacture
	r is aware of the performance criteria of their products as specified in t
	he contract documents. Confirm there are no defects and the installation o
	f the WRB membrane within 4' of fenestration's to be tested. Confirm windo
	w & door installations are complete\, including all caulk joints\, seals\,
	 flashing's\, hardware\, screens if provided\, etc. Siding shall not be in
	stalled at the time of testing. Confirm all interior air barrier sealants 
	are in place. Please ensure the operable windows and doors function proper
	ly. Check for level\, plumb and square in accordance with manufacturer’s
	 recommendations and ASTM 2112 guidelines. Work with BEE to establish wate
	r source\, confirm adequate water pressure and a nearby for source of elec
	trical power. Notify trades who may be working in the testing area. In the
	 event of a failure\, as specified by ASTM E1105\, remediation protocol sh
	all be established and submitted to BEE Consulting for approval and update
	 the project file. Failed Specimens shall be re-tested plus 3 additional s
	pecimens of like configuration. Contractor to schedule testing with BEE Co
	nsulting in the event of a failure.\n\n
DTEND;TZID="Pacific Standard Time":20230424T150000
