	><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-family:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-seri
	f">Nate W/ BEE 206-409-3240</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><s
	pan style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-family:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">
	&nbsp\;</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size
	:12.0pt\;font-family:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">Scope:</span><o:p></
	o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-family:
	&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">Pretalk for window testing\n</span><o:p><
	/o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-family
	:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">&nbsp\;</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p class=
	"MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-family:&quot\;Arial&quot\;
	\,sans-serif">Locations:</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp
	\;<o:p></o:p></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">Exact water infiltration testing l
	ocations are still a bit open-ended. Please confirm the exact desired floo
	rs for testing so we can schedule BEE:<o:p></o:p></p>\n<ul style="margin-t
	op:0in" type="disc">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\
	;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><b>North</b><o:p></o:p></li></ul>\n<ul style="ma
	rgin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="circle">\n<li
	 class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1"
	>CDC suggested levels 2\, 3\, or 4 for chamber testing.\n<b>Level 2</b> wo
	uld allow for the easiest and safest access. Is this acceptable?<o:p></o:p
	></li></ul>\n</ul>\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<li class="Ms
	oListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><b>West</
	b><o:p></o:p></li></ul>\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<ul styl
	e="margin-top:0in" type="circle">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="mar
	gin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1">CDC suggested Levels 5\, 6\, 8\, or
	 9 for chamber testing.\n<b>Level 5</b> would allow for the easiest and sa
	fest access. Is this acceptable?<o:p></o:p></li></ul>\n</ul>\n<ul style="m
	argin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-le
	ft:0in\;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><b>East</b><o:p></o:p></li></ul>\n<ul sty
	le="margin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="circle"
	>\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 level2
	 lfo1">CDC did not recommend a level for chamber testing on this elevation
	.\n<b>Level 4</b> would allow for the easiest and safest access. Is this a
	cceptable?<o:p></o:p></li></ul>\n</ul>\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="d
	isc">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 le
	vel1 lfo1"><b>SW Corner (2 tests here requested)</b><o:p></o:p></li></ul>\
	n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type="disc">\n<ul style="margin-top:0in" type=
	"circle">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l
	0 level2 lfo1">On the lower levels\, CDC recommended testing levels 5 or 6
	.\n<b>Level 5</b> would be easiest and safest to access\, is this acceptab
	le for testing the SW corner?<o:p></o:p></li><li class="MsoListParagraph" 
	style="margin-left:0in\;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1">On the upper levels\, CDC
	 recommended testing levels 8 or 9. Access for both floors would be simila
	r. Is testing\n<b>Level 8</b> acceptable in the SW corner?<o:p></o:p></li>
	</ul>\n</ul>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;font-fam
	ily:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">Contact:</span><o:p></o:p></p>\n<p cl
	ass="MsoNormal"><b><span style="font-size:10.5pt\;font-family:&quot\;FrnkG
	othITC Bk BT&quot\;\;color:#949CA1\;letter-spacing:1.0pt">William Jefferso
	n</span></b><span style="font-size:10.5pt\;font-family:&quot\;FrnkGothITC 
