CATEGORIES:Window Testing
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20231212T230705Z
DESCRIPTION:See below information\n\n \n\n*	Interior finishes will be comin
	g off and we will be testing (1) SH and (1) Pic in Unit 103.  Both of thes
	e are a PG-30\, which equates to 3 PSF with the 1/3rd reduction applied ag
	ainst 15% of the DP.  While BEE does not typically apply the 1/3rd reducti
	on\, it is in direct accord with AAMA 502 and Milgard should appreciate th
	e latitude in the event we do wind up having to engage with them re: the r
	esults.\n*	Interior finishes will consist of the sheet rock extension jamb
	s\, with this excavation being done up to an 1” or so from the interior 
	edges so that we can maintain the corner beads at the sheet rock.  Test te
	am\, if this is going to be a problem please let us know.\n*	As discussed 
	with CDK\, this test is a perfect “drop in” in the event we have cance
	llations prior to our official test date.  If CDK can prioritize removing 
	these finishes we would then have more potential to get this done sooner!\
	n*	Please have Exterior Makers hold off on siding E. L1 until after the te
	st is done.  This will allow us to potentially select other specimens to t
	est if the results of the first test warrant it.  Having CDK staff standin
	g by over the duration of the test will be very useful and is encouraged.\
	n*	Lastly\, while my belief that Milgard likely won’t be too keen on sup
	porting us here hasn’t changed\, I think it actually would be useful to 
	put together a documented invite to them when we know we have a test date 
	scheduled.  They may very well ignore it but they would never be able to s
	ay they were left in the dark and\, who knows\, could even decide to parti
	cipate!  CDK\, they would essentially be one of your de facto “vendors
	” on the project so is this something you can put together when the time
	 comes?\n\n \n\n \n\n
