SUMMARY;LANGUAGE=en-us:HARVARD COURT Window Test 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
UID:040000008200E00074C5B7101A82E0080000000047B693843F0FD901000000000000000
	010000000785111F612543A4F8BB715E9F78FA3D9
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><head>\n<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" 
	content="text/html\; charset=Windows-1252">\n<meta name="Generator" conten
	t="Microsoft Word 15 (filtered medium)">\n<style>\n<!--\n@font-face\n	{fon
	t-family:Wingdings}\n@font-face\n	{font-family:"Cambria Math"}\n@font-face
	\n	{font-family:Calibri}\np.MsoNormal\, li.MsoNormal\, div.MsoNormal\n	{ma
	rgin:0in\;\n	font-size:11.0pt\;\n	font-family:"Calibri"\,sans-serif}\np.Ms
	oListParagraph\, li.MsoListParagraph\, div.MsoListParagraph\n	{margin-top:
	0in\;\n	margin-right:0in\;\n	margin-bottom:0in\;\n	margin-left:.5in\;\n	fo
	nt-size:11.0pt\;\n	font-family:"Calibri"\,sans-serif}\nspan.EmailStyle17\n
		{font-family:"Arial"\,sans-serif\;\n	color:windowtext\;\n	font-weight:nor
	mal\;\n	font-style:normal\;\n	text-decoration:none none}\n.MsoChpDefault\n
		{font-family:"Calibri"\,sans-serif}\n@page WordSection1\n	{margin:1.0in 1
	.0in 1.0in 1.0in}\ndiv.WordSection1\n	{}\nol\n	{margin-bottom:0in}\nul\n	{
	margin-bottom:0in}\n-->\n</style>\n</head>\n<body lang="EN-US" link="#0563
	C1" vlink="#954F72" style="word-wrap:break-word">\n<div class="WordSection
	1">\n<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left:.5in\; text-indent:-.25in">Se
	e below information</p>\n<p class="MsoListParagraph">&nbsp\;</p>\n<ul type
	="disc" style="margin-top:0in">\n<li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margi
	n-left:0in">Interior finishes will be coming off and we will be testing (1
	) SH and (1) Pic in Unit 103.&nbsp\; Both of these are a PG-30\, which equ
	ates to 3 PSF with the 1/3<sup>rd</sup> reduction applied against 15% of t
	he\n DP.&nbsp\; While BEE does not typically apply the 1/3<sup>rd</sup> re
	duction\, it is in direct accord with AAMA 502 and Milgard should apprecia
	te the latitude in the event we do wind up having to engage with them re: 
	the results.</li><li class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0in">Inte
	rior finishes will consist of the sheet rock extension jambs\, with this e
	xcavation being done up to an 1” or so from the interior edges so that w
	e can maintain the corner beads at the sheet rock.&nbsp\; Test\n team\, if
	 this is going to be a problem please let us know.</li><li class="MsoListP
	aragraph" style="margin-left:0in">As discussed with CDK\, this test is a p
	erfect “drop in” in the event we have cancellations prior to our offic
	ial test date.&nbsp\; If CDK can prioritize removing these finishes we wou
	ld then have more potential\n to get this done sooner!</li><li class="MsoL
	istParagraph" style="margin-left:0in">Please have Exterior Makers hold off
	 on siding E. L1 until after the test is done.&nbsp\; This will allow us t
	o potentially select other specimens to test if the results of the first t
	est warrant it.&nbsp\; Having CDK\n staff standing by over the duration of
	 the test will be very useful and is encouraged.</li><li class="MsoListPar
	agraph" style="margin-left:0in">Lastly\, while my belief that Milgard like
	ly won’t be too keen on supporting us here hasn’t changed\, I think it
	 actually would be useful to put together a documented invite to them when
	 we know we have a test\n date scheduled.&nbsp\; They may very well ignore
	 it but they would never be able to say they were left in the dark and\, w
	ho knows\, could even decide to participate!&nbsp\; CDK\, they would essen
	tially be one of your de facto “vendors” on the project so is this som
	ething\n you can put together when the time comes?</li></ul>\n<p class="Ms
	oNormal">&nbsp\;</p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt\;
	 font-family:&quot\;Arial&quot\;\,sans-serif">&nbsp\;</span></p>\n</div>\n
	</body>\n</html>\n
