CREATED:20241113T000829Z
DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Torin\, Robbie\, Dave\, Jesus\, & Chris 425-595-7654
	\n\n \n\nScope- 289-unit building\, three separate test zones (main buildi
	ng\, retail spaces\, single live-work unit). BEE will arrive onsite at 7am
	 and begin setting up test equipment\, testing will begin at 1pm at which 
	time all personnel must leave the building for the duration of the testing
	 ~ 1.5 hours.\n\n \n\nNotes- \n\nBuilding prep (HVAC isolation) to be comp
	leted 2/10-2/12. Responsible party for building prep TBD. \n\n \n\nAll ext
	erior doors\, and doors leading to unconditioned spaces will need to be in
	stalled with hardware and gaskets including\, thresholds\, and fire caulki
	ng exit doors.\n\n \n\nAll penetrations in the envelope will need to be se
	aled including\, holes or tears in the WRB\, pipe penetrations from exteri
	or and unconditioned spaces\, and penetrations to the commercial spaces.\n
	\n \n\nAll gaps in the storefront need to be sealed and all missing glass 
	needs to be installed\, complete with gaskets.\n\n \n\nThe fan placement f
	or the main portion of the building will be in the two double doors on L4 
	in the courtyard. Will need 7 outlets near them to power the equipment. Sp
	ider boxes will work as long as there are two at each location\, if there 
	is permanent power to the building we can use circuits in units and no spi
	der boxes will be needed.\n\n \n\nAll drains and P-traps need to be filled
	 with water prior to the testing date.\n\n \n\nContact- George Goff w/ Jod
	y Miller Construction – 253-906-4150\n\n \n\n
DTEND;TZID="Pacific Standard Time":20250213T170000
DTSTAMP:20250107T172617Z
