	\n<p class="MsoNormal">Attendees- Jesus Garcia &amp\; Dave Luxmore (425-34
	5-9656)</p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp\;</p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">Scope:
	 ASTM E1105 testing on 3 Casement Windows and 3 Sliding Glass Doors (or am
	ount left on project if less than three).</p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp\
	;</p>\n<p class="MsoNormal">Test Pressure- 4.5 PSF</p>\n<p class="MsoNorma
	l"><span style="font-size:12.0pt">&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"
	><span style="font-size:12.0pt">Note- GC to invite window manufacturer to 
	the testing date. There should be a completed field of WRB surrounding the
	 test locations\, interior air barrier sealant in place\, head flashing in
	stalled\, a power\n source (standard outlet)\, a water source\, and interi
	or/exterior access to the test locations.</span></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"
	><span style="font-size:12.0pt">&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><
	span style="font-size:12.0pt">Contact-</span></p>\n<p class="MsoNormal"><s
	pan style="font-size:12.0pt">Dean Gorby | Carrig Construction | C. 425.628
	.8162 | www.carrigconstruction.com</span></p>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n
