DESCRIPTION:\nAttendee(s):\n\nJesus Garcia\n\nBEE Engineers\n\n425-900-3793
	\n\nRobert Smith\n\nBEE Engineers\n\n425-344-6997\n\n\nScope:\n\n\nASTM E1
	105 - Procedure B: cyclic static air pressure difference testing on (2) Fi
	xed Windows & (2} Sliding Doors\n\n\ntest specification(s)\n\n\nTest press
	ure: 2/3 of product laboratory rated pressure \n\nSliding glass doors DP 3
	5 (5.43PSF) = 3.62PSF with reduction \n\nFixed Windows DP50 (7.52PSF) = 5.
	01 PSF with reduction \n\nPressure Cycles: 4 (5 minutes of static pressure
	 with 1 minute of ambient pressure between)\n\n\nTest location(s)\n\n\nFix
	ed windows – Level 2\, Guestroom(s)\n\n\n\n \n\nSliding Doors – Level 
	3\, Guestroom(s)\n\n\n\n \n\n\nNote:\n\n\nGC to invite window manufacturer
	 (Pella Windows) to testing date. All test locations should be installed t
	o detail and have interior air barrier sealant in place.\n\n\non-site cont
	act:\n\n\n \n\nRyan Hogan | Project Manager\nSIERRA CONSTRUCTION COMPANY\,
	 INC.\np. 425-487-5200 | c. 206-579-7348 | www.sierraind.com <https://urld
