DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Torin (425-595-7654)\, Robbie\, Dave\, Jesus\, & Chr
	is \n\n \n\nScope- Building prep/HVAC isolations for air barrier testing o
	n a 271-unit building. BEE will arrive onsite at 7:30am and begin sealing 
	off the HVAC in the units and prepping the building for the air barrier te
	sting. Breakers for ERV units will be shut off during the prep\, and the u
	nit doors will be propped open upon completion of prep.\n\n \n\nNote- GC t
	o notify Subcontractors to not remove the blue plastic covering the HVAC o
	r turn breakers on while HVAC is covered. All exterior doors must be insta
	lled with hardware\, gaskets\, and thresholds. All storefronts to be compl
	eted with all glass\, gaskets\, and sealants in place. All demising walls 
	that separate conditioned from non-conditioned areas must be completed. Wa
	ter must be in all drain P-traps to avoid excessive air leakage from the s
	ewers. Please let BEE know if you need to reschedule this testing as soon 
	as possible.\n\n \n\nContact-\n\nRiley Martin\n\nSuperintendent\n\n <http:
	//stsconstructionservices.com/> \n\nRileyM@stsconst.com <mailto:RileyM@sts
	const.com> \n\n206.775.9887 Cell\n\n206.439.6343 Office\n\n \n\n
