CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20251201T235444Z
DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Torin Garner (425-595-7654)\, Robbie Smith\, Dave Lu
	xmore\, Jesus Garcia\, & Chris Shafer\n\n \n\nScope- ASTM-E779. Air barrie
	r testing a 316-unit building. BEE will arrive onsite at 7:00am and begin 
	setting up test equipment\, testing will begin at 1pm at which time all pe
	rsonnel not directly involved with the testing crew must leave the buildin
	g for the duration of the testing ~ 1-2 hours.\n\n \n\nNotes- \n\nIn order
	 to perform the testing\, the elevator doors must be opened on elevator A 
	on L3-L7 (car parked on L2 or lower) and on elevator B on L3 & L2 to provi
	de adequate airflow for the testing throughout the building (since there i
	s only 1 interior stairwell). Barricades should be placed in front of the 
	shafts prior to opening. Elevator Doors to be opened once the building is 
	cleared of all personnel not involved with the testing crew.\n\nAll exteri
	or doors must have thresholds\, gaskets\, AB sealant\, & hardware installe
	d. \n\nWater must be in all drain P traps or the drains taped off. \n\nAll
	 penetrations through walls from conditioned to unconditioned spaces to be
	 sealed (fire caulk or similar). Top and bottom plates of these demising w
	all recommended to be sealed as well.\n\nFans will be placed in the L3 cou
	rtyards\, power will be used from surrounding units. \n\nAll HVAC in the b
	uilding must be off and sealed prior to the test. \n\nAHB/ACG has chosen t
	o sub out the building prep\, the GC is responsible for ensuring the sub h
	as all HVAC penetrations throughout the building (Roof\, unit HVAC\, commo
	n areas\, L1 louvers\, vestibules\, retail spaces\, parking garage areas\,
	 fireplaces\, trash chutes\, ect) are fully covered (with proper materials
	 such as Bron blue grill mask or Retrotec yellow gill mask) in accordance 
	with 2018 WA State energy code requirements in addition to propping all in
	terior doors and ensuring all exterior windows and doors are shut prior to
	 the 1pm test time. \n\nLint traps in dryers (if installed) must be sealed
	\, if dryers aren’t installed the dryer vent must be sealed. \n\nMicrowa
	ve range hoods must be sealed and doors taped (3” painter tape is what w
	e use) shut (this includes the top vent). \n\nPTAC’s must be completely 
	sealed around the perimeter and the vents to ensure no extraneous air leak
	age. \n\nERV vents to be sealed (to the drywall not just the grille) and E
	RV to be inspected for unused air ducts (if present must be sealed) that m
	ay cause extraneous leakage as well as the access hatches sealed (painters
	 tape recommended). \n\nBEE will survey the prep for general compliance wi
	th code but cannot be responsible for missed or inadequate preparation of 
	the building. \n\nPer 2018 WSEC the target pass fail rate 0.25 CFM/SQFT at
	 75 Pa\, a failure of over 0.40 CFM/SQFT at 75 Pa will require retesting.\
	n\n \n\nContact-\n\nJustin Thomas\n\nSuperintendent\n\nAmerican Home Build
	ers\, Inc\n\np: 206.638-0588 e: jthomas@acg.com <mailto:jthomas@acg.com> \
	n\n \n\n
