	L3 courtyards\, power will be used from surrounding units. <o:p></o:p></p>
	<p class=MsoNormal>All HVAC in the building must be off and sealed prior t
	o the test. <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>AHB/ACG has chosen to sub ou
	t the building prep\, the GC is responsible for ensuring the sub has all H
	VAC penetrations throughout the building (Roof\, unit HVAC\, common areas\
	, L1 louvers\, vestibules\, retail spaces\, parking garage areas\, firepla
	ces\, trash chutes\, ect) are fully covered (with proper materials such as
	 Bron blue grill mask or Retrotec yellow gill mask) in accordance with 201
	8 WA State energy code requirements in addition to propping all interior d
	oors and ensuring all exterior windows and doors are shut prior to the 1pm
	 test time. <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>Lint traps in dryers (if ins
	talled) must be sealed\, if dryers aren&#8217\;t installed the dryer vent 
	must be sealed. <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>Microwave range hoods mu
	st be sealed and doors taped (3&#8221\; painter tape is what we use) shut 
	(this includes the top vent). <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>PTAC&#8217
	\;s must be completely sealed around the perimeter and the vents to ensure
	 no extraneous air leakage. <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>ERV vents to
	 be sealed (to the drywall not just the grille) and ERV to be inspected fo
	r unused air ducts (if present must be sealed) that may cause extraneous l
	eakage as well as the access hatches sealed (painters tape recommended). <
	o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>BEE will survey the prep for general comp
	liance with code but cannot be responsible for missed or inadequate prepar
	ation of the building. <o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>Per 2018 WSEC the
	 target pass fail rate 0.25 CFM/SQFT at 75 Pa\, a failure of over 0.40 CFM
	/SQFT at 75 Pa will require retesting.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal><o
	:p>&nbsp\;</o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal>Contact-<o:p></o:p></p><p style='ms
	o-margin-top-alt:12.0pt\;margin-right:0in\;margin-bottom:12.0pt\;margin-le
	ft:0in\;background:white'><b><span style='font-size:11.0pt\;color:black'>J
	ustin Thomas</span></b><o:p></o:p></p><p style='mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt\
	;margin-right:0in\;margin-bottom:12.0pt\;margin-left:0in\;background:white
	'><b><span style='font-size:10.0pt\;color:black'>Superintendent</span></b>
	<o:p></o:p></p><p style='mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt\;margin-right:0in\;marg
	in-bottom:12.0pt\;margin-left:0in\;background:white'><b><span style='font-
	size:10.0pt\;color:#4472C4'>American Home Builders\, Inc</span></b><o:p></
	o:p></p><p style='mso-margin-top-alt:12.0pt\;margin-right:0in\;margin-bott
	om:12.0pt\;margin-left:0in\;background:white'><span style='font-size:10.0p
	t\;color:#A0A4AA'>p: 206.638-0588 e:&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:jthomas@acg.com
	">jthomas@acg.com</a></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp\;
	</o:p></p></div></body></html>
