	h1><span style='font-size:14.0pt'>Scope:&nbsp\;<o:p></o:p></span></h1><p c
	lass=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto\;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto'
	>ASTM E1105 Window Water Penetration Resistance Testing. Retest the 2 fail
	ed 4-lite fixed windows in the L4 &amp\; L5 Hallway\, south elevation. 6 a
	dditional windows of the same type to be tested as well. 8 locations total
	.<o:p></o:p></p><h1><span style='font-size:14.0pt'>Test Pressure:&nbsp\;<o
	:p></o:p></span></h1><p class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto\;ms
	o-margin-bottom-alt:auto'>5.25 PSF for Windows<o:p></o:p></p><h1><span sty
	le='font-size:14.0pt'>Note:&nbsp\;<o:p></o:p></span></h1><p class=MsoNorma
	l style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto\;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto'>GC recommend
	ed to invite installer to testing date. Test locations to have a completed
	 field of WRB surrounding them\, head flashing installed\, and interior ai
	r barrier sealant in place. No drywall or siding surrounding the test loca
	tions.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto\;ms
	o-margin-bottom-alt:auto'><b><u>ONSITE CONTACT: </u></b>Gary Rush<b> </b>(
	661)-444-0662<o:p></o:p></p><p class=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp\;</o:p></p><p cl
	ass=MsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp\;</o:p></p></div></body></html>
