DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Torin Garner (425-595-7654)\, Chris Shafer\, & Dave 
	Luxmore\n\n \n\nScope- ASTM E779. Air barrier testing 1 TI space (roughly 
	12k sqft). BEE will arrive at 9am and begin prepping the building and sett
	ing up test equipment in the large TI\, at 9am all personnel not involved 
	with the test must exit the building for the duration of the testing ~45 m
	ins. \n\n \n\nNote- All doors should have gaskets and hardware installed\,
	 all penetrations into the air barrier should be sealed\, water should be 
	in all drains\, & the building envelope should be completed prior to the t
	esting date. All HVAC in the TI Space should be shut off upon BEE’s arri
	val.\n\n \n\nContact-\n\nRob Overton\n\nProject Manager\nSIERRA CONSTRUCTI
	ON COMPANY\, INC.\n\n14800 NE North Woodinville Way\, Woodinville\, WA 980
	72\no. 425-487-5200 | c. 425-219-0997\n\nwww.sierraind.com <http://www.sie
	rraind.com> \n\n \n\n
