DESCRIPTION:Attendees- Dave Luxmore (425-345-9656) & Jesus Betancourt\n\n \
	n\nScope- ASTM E1105. 1 horizontal slider\, 1 sliding glass door\, 1 fixed
	 window\, & 1 casement. 4 locations total.\n\n \n\nTest Pressure- 2/3 of l
	ab rating. TBD.\n\n \n\nFailure protocol outlined on project drawings is t
	o test 5 additional test locations of the same type if a failure occurs. T
	his would require an additional testing day at a later date.\n\n \n\nNote-
	GC would like to test locations with siding in place. Cornerstone prefers 
	window screens installed if available for prospective test locations. GC t
	o provide adequate water and power sources near prospective test locations
	.\n\n \n\nContact-\n\n <https://www.olsenanderson.com/about> \n\nWill Feli
	x\n\nAssistant Superintendent\n\nOffice: 206.565.2815 | Cell: 425.891.3449
	\n\nwill@olsenanderson.com <mailto:will@olsenanderson.com%0d> \n\n1148 NW 
	Leary Way | Seattle\, WA 98107\n\n \n\n
DTEND;TZID="Pacific Standard Time":20260612T150000
